course: dictionary
lesson: 2839
title: Djinn: a spirit from stories
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A djinn is a spirit, not a person. Muslims believe djinn are real beings created by God, and in storybooks they are magic spirits who grant wishes. «His magic ring could call up Djinns, Fairies and even a great angel.» The clue is call up: the Djinns come when he calls them, like helpers who obey him.
explain: The word can be spelt in different ways, and context helps you see they mean the same thing. It can be djinn, jinn, jinni or genie. «The Djinn said, "You will be able to work now for three days without eating..."» The Djinn speaks like a wise teacher, so in this story it is not a monster to fear.
explain: Capital letters are a clue too. Kipling writes «the Djinn in charge of All Deserts» with capitals, the way a sign uses capitals for a title. The big D tells you this Djinn is an important character, not just any spirit.
fact: A djinn is a spirit made of smokeless fire, found in Arab and Muslim stories and beliefs.
fact: A djinn can be good or bad, and can sometimes take the shape of people or animals.
fact: A genie, like the magic spirit in the lamp in Aladdin, is another name for a djinn.
fact: In «How the Camel Got His Hump», the Djinn gives the lazy Camel a hump because he only says «Humph!» and will not work.
fact: Djinn, jinn, jinni and genie are different spellings or words for the same kind of spirit.
exercise: What is a djinn, in the sense of a spirit from Arab and Muslim stories? | *A spirit made of smokeless fire, which can be good or bad | A kind of fast horse | A type of stone lamp | A pale fish
exercise: In the Just So Story, why does the Djinn give the Camel a hump? | It was a birthday present | *Because the lazy Camel only says «Humph!» and will not work | Because the Camel was kind to the Djinn | Because the Camel asked for a hump
exercise: Kipling writes «the Djinn in charge of All Deserts» with capital letters. Why? | Because it is the start of a sentence | Because the Camel wrote it | By mistake, like a spelling error | *To make it sound grand and important
test: Which word is another name for a djinn, like the spirit in the story of Aladdin? | Ghoul | *Genie | Giant | Goblin
test: In «turned once, Afrits and Djinns came out of the earth», what does turned once do? | Nothing happens at all | It makes the ring lighter | *It calls up Afrits and Djinns from the earth | It makes the ring hot
exam: What is the Camel's hump used for in the story? | *To store food so he can work three days without eating | To hold water like a bottle | To hold a fan on hot days | To make him run faster
